 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Boundary Conditions:** Values outside the octree data are defined to be zero [S4]. Implementers must handle cases where forward neighbors lie outside the defined volume bounds.
-- **Precision:** The logical shift of half a voxel width must be handled carefully to avoid floating-point errors, especially at boundaries [S1, S2, S3].
-- **Degenerate Input:** If the octree is empty or contains no leaves, no intersections are returned [S5].
+- **Boundary Conditions:** Values outside the octree data are defined to be zero [S4]. Implementers must handle cases where forward neighbors lie outside the defined volume bounds by returning zero values [S4].
+- **Neighbor-Finding Cost:** Neighbor-finding on octrees is computationally intensive compared to array indexing [S1, S2, S3]. The worst-case complexity is O(log N), but it skews heavily toward O(1) when neighbors lie within the same parent [S1, S2, S3].
+- **Point Location Overhead:** Querying neighbors in an octree is more intensive than in a 3D array, requiring full top-down point location from the root in the worst case [S1, S2, S3].
 
